        "start_xml_ordinal": 19253,
        "body_paragraph_zero_based": 717,
        "direct_body_paragraph_zero_based": 368,
        "paragraph_id": null,
        "text": "Where  and is determined by the linear dispersion relation. As only waves with a small steepness are considered the depth averaged velocities can be approximated safely with linear wave theory and are given by:"
      }
    ],
    "following_nonempty_paragraphs": [
      {
        "container_path": "_staging/total-read/model-audit/XBeach/connectivity/nonhydro-read/body-field-recovery/body-cached.docx",
        "member": "word/document.xml",
        "start_xml_ordinal": 19370,
        "body_paragraph_zero_based": 719,
        "direct_body_paragraph_zero_based": 370,
        "paragraph_id": null,
        "text": "The velocity field and the surface elevation at t=0s are used as initial conditions for the test. The basin length is set at  with a relative depth of kH=0.5. The basin is discretized using  gridpoints with a CFL condition of 0.5."
      },
      {
        "container_path": "_staging/total-read/model-audit/XBeach/connectivity/nonhydro-read/body-field-recovery/body-cached.docx",
        "member": "word/document.xml",
        "start_xml_ordinal": 19449,
        "body_paragraph_zero_based": 721,
        "direct_body_paragraph_zero_based": 372,
        "paragraph_id": null,
        "text": "Figure 4-10 a-b shows model results of the free surface and velocity in x = (1,1). For both the velocities and the free surface the amplitude is correctly modelled for the five periods shown. There does appear to be a slight increase in period but this is to be expected from (2.1). In Figure 4-11 contours are shown for four different times during the first half of the fourth period, together with the velocity vectors and the contours of the analytical solution. Aside from the difference in phase the numerical solution reproduces the correct behaviour. The solution stays symmetric around the diagonals and the velocity pattern is correct"
      }
    ],
    "table_cell": null,
    "text_method": "Saved display-field substitution plus w:t; equation objects are not transcribed."
  },
